  "coverage_qualification": [
    "All thirteen original source groups were reviewed against printed pp.372\u2013373. No in-book mathematical paragraph was omitted; only the pointer to the stronger later 4.1.20 theorem remains prose.",
    "The independently specified radial shrink is opaque after existence. Both printed squared-norm displays, the nonpositive difference and every inner, mixed and boundary case are retained.",
    "Actual normalized convolutions agree on the original closed-ball locus. Its valid original local convolution domain is open. The two-parameter errors, common differential bounds and fixed-radius eventual capture are proved.",
    "The intermediate modified maps take values in the ambient Euclidean space. Compact target margins derive a common source where the eventual smooth maps lie in the original open target, without convexity or a global target-valued extension.",
    "The final support-only coincidence assumes arbitrary original flat currents. It adds no normality, finite mass, equality on the compact flat index or flat membership indexed by the support.",
    "The original Lipschitz retraction is given only on compact K. Its compact image and neighbourhood extension are derived; no whole-domain retraction is required. Empty retracts remain allowed.",
